A||||3||Borgio||I too almost died||||1||
Z||000000||Borgio||11-14-2001||10:42 PM||||I have a story similar to Crashes, except I didn't do it on purpose.<P>My brother and I were going to a camp out in the country we were driving down a country road in his 2m4. He always had the pedal to the floor in this car since it was a 4 banger and he had to floor it all the time to get any excitement. <BR>Anyway, so it was a fairly nice road for a country road. We were going about 90mph, and out of nowhere there was a railroad crossing. Actually, there was a set of railroad tracks with a dip in the middle. The bump was literally about 5 feet high. <BR>We only got slowed down to about 80. We hit the bump and flew into the air. While we were probably only slightly of the ground and in the air for a fraction of a second, it felt like we were 20ft in the air and like it lasted an eternity, holding on for dear life. HANG TIME. We tipped slightly in the air, the left front corner hit first. We actually landed totally in the other lane. But we didn’t wreck, so it was awesome.<BR> I would NEVER do it again though.  This bump was crazy, it is VERY dangerous and they (the county) should definitely do something about it.<BR> I went over it later in my parents van remembering the situation and knowing to take it slow. I went over it at 30mph and the van jolted downward and the front bumper smashed into the ground. So in essence I did do it again. <BR>It was an amazing experience, the scariest of my life. Words can’t adequately describe the situation and the feeling.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Borgio (edited 11-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||loafer87gt||11-14-2001||11:00 PM||||Yeah, you have to watch out for those RR tracks! I can still remember countless numbers of cropchecks out in hickville Saskatchewan when me and my buddies launched a 1/2 ton truck into a slough or off a deadend road after hitting a set of tracks flat out. Gawd we were stupid when we were young, one time we cranked a tree that was lying across the road and my buddies bottle of home brew flew up and went through the windshield. It was kinda hard explaining how that happened to my folks, I don't think my Dad bought the pepsi bottle story.||||reg||1
Z||000002||dennis_6||11-15-2001||03:15 AM||||I did that on accident in a 1990 Corsica once 85mph on hickville, Ohio roads.  Hit a very nice bump that had a nice drop following behind it and went airborne.   It was fun nothing better than back roads in southern Ohio.  But I will not ever do that again on purpose.  Corsica pulled to one side real hard after that.  Never figured out why.  Maybe it just needed some nitrous.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChopTop||11-15-2001||02:27 PM||||Reminds me of my schoolbus days.  I lived in a rural area and we had to go over railroad tracks everyday on a dirt road.  The bus was generally deserted and several of us would make our way to the back of the bus as the bus approached the tracks, always hollering at the driver, faster, faster!  Depending on his mood we'd either pop up a couple inches or a couple feet.  Sometimes someone would get hurt but we would never complain because we had asked for it.||||reg||1
